{"task":{"id":"Prob146_fsm_serialdata","spec":"
I would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following
interface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise
specified.

 - input  clk
 - input  in
 - input  reset
 - output out_byte (8 bits)
 - output done

In many (older) serial communications protocols, each data byte is sent
along with a start bit and a stop bit, to help the receiver delimit bytes
from the stream of bits. One common scheme is to use one start bit (0), 8
data bits, and 1 stop bit (1). The line is also at logic 1 when nothing
is being transmitted (idle). Design a finite state machine that will
identify when bytes have been correctly received when given a stream of
bits. It needs to identify the start bit, wait for all 8 data bits, then
verify that the stop bit was correct. The module will also output the
correctly-received data byte. `out_byte` needs to be valid when `done` is
1, and is don't-care otherwise. If the stop bit does not appear when
expected, the FSM must wait until it finds a stop bit before attempting
to receive the next byte. Include a active-high synchronous reset. Note
that the serial protocol sends the least significant bit first. It should
assert done each time it finds a stop bit. Assume all sequential logic is
triggered on the positive edge of the clock.

","interface":{"top":"TopModule","ports":[{"name":"clk","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"in","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"reset","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"out_byte","direction":"output","width":8,"signed":false},{"name":"done","direction":"output","width":1,"signed":false}]},"constraints":"SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."},"current":{"revision_id":"3bc4bfa7-5b53-4282-9ca6-e10a02eed9bf","source_sha256":"223efeb1e2ffaa09ce1e73b89e3caa45518fe6771d60b961fa7fcff612e9d9c5","source":"
module TopModule (
    input clk,
    input in,
    input reset,
    output reg [7:0] out_byte,
    output wire done
);

    localparam IDLE  = 3'd0,
               START = 3'd1,
               DATA  = 3'd2,
               STOP  = 3'd3,
               WAIT  = 3'd4;

    reg [2:0] state, next_state;
    reg [3:0] bit_cnt;
    reg [7:0] data_reg;

    always @(*) begin
        case (state)
            IDLE:  next_state = in ? IDLE : START;
            START: next_state = DATA;
            DATA:  next_state = (bit_cnt == 4'd7) ? STOP : DATA;
            STOP:  next_state = in ? IDLE : WAIT;
            WAIT:  next_state = in ? IDLE : WAIT;
            default: next_state = IDLE;
        endcase
    end

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (reset) begin
            state    <= IDLE;
            bit_cnt  <= 4'd0;
            data_reg <= 8'd0;
            out_byte <= 8'd0;
        end else begin
            state <= next_state;

            case (state)
                IDLE: begin
                    bit_cnt <= 4'd0;
                end

                START: begin
                    data_reg[0] <= in;
                    bit_cnt     <= 4'd1;
                end

                DATA: begin
                    data_reg[bit_cnt] <= in;
                    if (bit_cnt == 4'd7)
                        bit_cnt <= 4'd0;
                    else
                        bit_cnt <= bit_cnt + 4'd1;
                end

                STOP: begin
                    if (in) begin
                        out_byte <= data_reg;
                    end
                end

                WAIT: begin
                    bit_cnt <= 4'd0;
                end

                default: begin
                    bit_cnt <= 4'd0;
                end
            endcase
        end
    end

    assign done = (state == STOP) && in;

endmodule
